## 1 · Schema

**Collection `orders`** — one per aggregate root, `@Document("orders")`, `@TypeAlias("order")`.

| Stored field | BSON type | Required | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `_id` | UUID (standard, subtype 4) | yes | assigned by the application, UUIDv7 |
| `orderNumber` | string | yes | business key — unique index |
| `customerId` | UUID | yes | another aggregate: its id only, never a reference |
| `status` | string | yes | enum by name: `PLACED`, `CONFIRMED`, `CANCELLED` |
| `total` | decimal128 | no | absent in shape 1 — upcast on read |
| `lines` | array of `{sku, quantity, unitPrice}` | yes | embedded child entities; **bound 200** — the aggregate refuses more, the validator caps it |
| `placedAt` | date | yes | an `Instant` |
| `schemaVersion` | int | yes | current shape: 2 |
| `version` | long | yes | `@Version` — inserts on `null`, updates with the version in the filter |

**Indexes**

| Index | Keys | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `_id_` | `_id` | created with the collection |
| `ux_orders_order_number` | `orderNumber` asc, **unique** | the business key; serves `existsByOrderNumber` |
| `ix_orders_customer_placed` | `customerId` asc, `placedAt` desc, `_id` desc | the customer's listing: filter, sort and keyset tiebreaker in one index |

**Validator** — `$jsonSchema`, `validationAction: error`: the required fields above, `status` in its
three values, `lines` at most 200 items, `placedAt` a date, `schemaVersion` an int.

**Personal data at rest** — `@.claude/rules/personal-data.md` § At rest.

| Field | Holds | Retention | Why it is stored at all |
|---|---|---|---|
| — | no field holds personal data; the customer is referenced by id | — | — |

**Transactions.** The case writes `orders` and appends `OrderPlaced` to `outbox_events` in one
transaction, through `DocumentTransactions` on the `mongoTransactionManager`; the server is a
replica set in every environment. A transient error retries the whole transaction up to three times,
then `ConflictException`.

**Claim strategy — `outbox_events` only.** Lease per document by `findAndModify`
(`claimedUntil`, 60 s), so `35-jobs.md` § 3's 2 replicas never take the same event inside the lease.

## 2 · Mapping

Aggregate `Order` → document `OrderDocument` in `adapter/out/persistence/order`, lines embedded as
`OrderLineDocument` records. Package-private, one subpackage per aggregate.

| Aggregate field | Domain type | Stored field | Translation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | `OrderId` | `_id` | `OrderId.value()` ↔ `new OrderId(uuid)` |
| `number` | `String` | `orderNumber` | direct |
| `customerId` | `CustomerId` | `customerId` | `.value()` ↔ `new CustomerId(uuid)` |
| `total` | `BigDecimal` | `total` | direct; shape 1 → sum of the lines (upcast) |
| `lines` | `List<OrderLine>` | `lines` | per item, both ways |
| — | — | `schemaVersion`, `version` | document-only, invisible to the domain |

## 3 · Adapter and ports

| Port | Signature (from `10-domain.md`) | Operation | Index serving it |
|---|---|---|---|
| `CreateOrderPort` | `Order create(Order order)` | insert (`version` null) — `DuplicateKeyException` → `ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS` | `_id_`, `ux_orders_order_number` |
| `SaveOrderPort` | `Order save(Order order)` | load, mutate, save with the stored version — `OptimisticLockingFailureException` → `ORDER_CONCURRENT_UPDATE` | `_id_` |
| `LoadOrderPort` | `Optional<Order> byId(OrderId id)` | find by `_id` | `_id_` |
| `ListCustomerOrdersPort` | `CustomerOrdersPage page(CustomerId, Optional<Cursor>, int)` | keyset `Window`, projection without lines | `ix_orders_customer_placed` |

## 4 · Migrations

No migration file: the collection's indexes and validator are declared in code and applied at
startup. The executor creates the file below from this block, verbatim.

**`src/main/java/com/example/demo/adapter/out/persistence/order/OrderCollection.java`** — shape
`templates/MongoCollections.java.example`: the three indexes of § 1 and the validator.

| Change | Kind | Content |
|---|---|---|
| shape 1 → 2 | upcast | `total` stored from now on; read as the sum of the lines when absent; written on the next save |
| backfill | none | no query filters or sorts by `total` — an upcast is enough |

## 5 · Configuration

| Property | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `spring.mongodb.uri` | `${MONGO_URI:mongodb://…@localhost:${MONGO_PORT:27017}/…?authSource=admin&directConnection=true}` | the compose replica set from the host |
| `spring.mongodb.representation.uuid` | `standard` | rule |
| `spring.data.mongodb.representation.big-decimal` | `decimal128` | rule |
| `app.mongodb.server-selection-timeout` / `connect-timeout` / `read-timeout` | `5s` / `3s` / `10s` | the driver's defaults are 30 s, 10 s and never |
| `app.mongodb.max-pool-size` / `max-pool-wait` | `50` / `2s` | two replicas, the expected rate |

Full shape in `templates/application-mongodb.yml.example`; client and transaction wiring in
`templates/MongoConfig.java.example` (this project has no JPA: `MongoTransactionConfig`).

